@flexiarg math-formalization/layer-cake-crossover-split
@title Layer-Cake Bound by a Crossover Split
@sigils [⚖️/比]
@keywords layer-cake, distribution-function, weak-type, Lorentz, rpow, lintegral, crossover, min-majorant, ENNReal
@audience lean-provers, analysts
@tone heuristic
@difficulty advanced
@subjects analysis, measure-theory
@instantiates math-informal/estimate-by-bounding

! conclusion:
  Turn a weak-type distribution bound into a local subcritical power-integral bound by integrating the minimum of the finite-volume and tail estimates on opposite sides of their crossover.

  + IF:
      A layer-cake identity reduces the goal to an integral of a level measure D(t), and available estimates give D(t) ≤ min(V, C/t).

  + HOWEVER:
      Either arm alone is non-integrable at one endpoint, and direct ENNReal algebra obscures the scalar improper-integral calculation.

  + THEN:
      Split the positive axis at A = C/V. Use D(t) ≤ V below A and D(t) ≤ C/t above A, convert each nonnegative finite piece from lintegral/ofReal to a real integral, evaluate the two rpow integrals, combine their scalar values, and only then transport the finite ENNReal bound back to integrability and a Bochner integral inequality.
      + LEAN:
        api[MeasureTheory.lintegral_rpow_eq_lintegral_meas_lt_mul]
        api[MeasureTheory.lintegral_union]
        api[MeasureTheory.ofReal_integral_eq_lintegral_ofReal]
        api[integral_rpow]
        api[integral_Ioi_rpow_of_lt]
        api[MeasureTheory.lintegral_ofReal_ne_top_iff_integrable]

  + BECAUSE:
      The crossover is where the two majorants agree; assigning each arm only to the endpoint where it is integrable preserves the sharp subcritical constant and isolates ENNReal transport from real-variable algebra.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Separate zero-volume and zero-tail cases before defining C/V.]
    next[Extract C/t from the weak-type supremum and combine it with restriction monotonicity.]
    next[Prove the scalar crossover lemma independently of the original function and measure space.]
